# Nothing here is checked in; both trees are written by build.mcpp on every
# build. See §14 of the graphics-stack design doc: an artifact produced at
# build time cannot disagree with the data it came from, which is the whole
# reason not to commit it.
mcpp/wlroots/target/
mcpp/wlroots/include/*
!mcpp/wlroots/include/.gitkeep
mcpp/wlroots/src/

# The PROJECT-LEVEL store. mcpp puts dependencies here instead of the global
# one when the workspace declares `[indices]` with a path — which is how this
# fork was developed against an unmerged index PR. It is a cache of other
# people's packages and has no business in this repo.
.mcpp/
compile_commands.json
mcpp.lock

# upstream/ is never filtered. cairo's fork learned this the hard way: a
# project's own .gitignore files take effect when a fork commits its tree, and
# five files that WERE in the release tarball got silently dropped. wlroots
# ships one .gitignore of its own, so the same guard applies here.
!upstream/**
